# Without this, `COPY . .` drops the host's node_modules on top of the one the
# image just installed. On Windows that is fatal rather than merely wasteful:
# the .bin shims are generated for the host, so `npm run build` dies with
# `node.exe: not found` inside a Linux container. CI never saw it because a
# fresh checkout has no node_modules — `make csp` and any local `docker build`
# did.
node_modules
dist
.astro
npm-debug.log*
test-results
playwright-report
